  "journal.hint.go_back": "You can go back a page by using [bold]Escape[/bold] key or the controller's [bold]B button[/bold]!",
  "journal.hint.trait_view": "You can press [bold]{{key}}[/bold] to show an icon over every crop with traits.\n\nHover over a crop to see its details, then press it again to hide the icons.",
  "journal.hint.parent_quality": "The higher quality the parent crop, the more likely its [link=trait][underline]traits[/underline][/link] are inherited when using the [link=seed_splicer][underline]Seed Splicer[/underline][/link]!",
  "journal.hint.adjacent_crops": "Planting adjacent crops that share the same [link=trait][underline]trait[/underline][/link] can be a helpful way to increase their tier!",
  "journal.hint.combination_parents": "Each half of a [link=combination_traits][underline]combination trait[/underline][/link] must come from a different parent. A crop that has both parts won't fuse on its own.",
  "journal.getting_started.title": "Getting Started",
  "journal.getting_started.intro": "Every crop you plant has a small chance to gain a [link=trait][underline]trait[/underline][/link] when it first sprouts.\n\nThese traits can make a crop grow faster, sell for more or even give an extra harvest. Some traits can even make crops survive outside their normal seasons!\n\nBe mindful that not every trait is helpful, however.",
  "journal.getting_started.mutagenic_fertilizer": "Mutagenic Fertilizer can be used to raise the chances of a trait appearing by allowing the crop to roll for mutations every night it's watered (until fully grown).",
  "journal.getting_started.mutagenic_fertilizer_shop": "This can be purchased from Pierre once you reach farming level {{level}}.",
  "journal.getting_started.neighbors": "Where you plant a crop also matters. When a plant mutates, it is much more likely to pick up a trait from adjacent crops [highlight]of the same type[/highlight].",
  "journal.getting_started.tiers_heading": "Trait Details",
  "journal.getting_started.tiers": "Some traits have tiers, which strengthens their effect as the rank increases.\n\nMutations that occur for crops with existing traits may increase their rank, where applicable.\n\n[bounce][bold]Hint:[/bold][/bounce] Planting adjacent crops that share the same trait can be a helpful way to increase their tier!",
  "journal.getting_started.trait_limit": "Seeds and crops can hold up to [highlight]three traits[/highlight].\n\nA mutation may replace one of a crop's existing traits instead of adding a new one. If the crop already has three traits, one of them is always replaced.\n\nSome traits, called [link=combination_traits][underline]combination traits[/underline][/link], can only be produced by using the [link=seed_splicer][underline]Seed Splicer[/underline][/link].\n\nThis notebook will automatically keep track of all discovered traits.",
  "journal.getting_started.propagating_heading": "Propagating Traits",
  "journal.getting_started.seed_maker": "To reliably propagate the same set of traits, you can utilize the Seed Maker. This machine is craftable at farming level {{level}}.",
  "journal.getting_started.seed_maker_traits": "The Seed Maker will preserve the traits when creating new seeds, allowing for repeated planting of the same strain.",
  "journal.getting_started.splicing_heading": "Splicing Traits",
  "journal.getting_started.seed_splicer": "Traits can be mixed together more reliably by using the Seed Splicer. This machine is craftable at farming level {{level}}.",
  "journal.getting_started.seed_splicer_traits": "The Seed Splicer lets you splice two crops [highlight]of the same type[/highlight] but of different strains, either mixing their traits together or removing unwanted ones.",
  "journal.trait_view_key_unbound": "the trait view key (set it in the config)",
  "journal.spotting_mutations.title": "Spotting Mutations",
  "journal.spotting_mutations.sparkles": "Fully grown crops that have mutated will sparkle until they're harvested, so keep an eye out for any glimmers in your fields.",
  "journal.spotting_mutations.badges": "Seeds and produce that have traits are marked with a small green badge in the top-right corner. Hover over them to see their traits (negative ones are highlighted in [color=Red]red[/color]).",
  "journal.spotting_mutations.trait_view": "You can press [bold]{{key}}[/bold] to show an icon over every crop with traits. Hover over a crop to see its details, then press it again to hide the icons.",
  "journal.spotting_mutations.hidden_traits": "Before a crop is fully grown, you will only see the traits it was planted with. Once it has finished growing, any new traits will be marked with \"[bounce][color=ForestGreen]{{newLabel}}[/color][/bounce]\".",
  "journal.selective_breeding.title": "Selective Breeding",
  "journal.selective_breeding.seed_maker": "Got a set of traits that you would like to keep growing? Put its produce into a Seed Maker!",
  "journal.selective_breeding.seed_maker_unlock": "The Seed Maker is craftable starting from farming level {{level}}.\n\n[bounce][bold]Note:[/bold][/bounce] Crops with the [link=trait_seedless][underline]Seedless[/underline][/link] trait are unable to be processed by the Seed Maker.",
  "journal.selective_breeding.seed_splicer": "The Seed Splicer lets you splice two crops [highlight]of the same type[/highlight] with different traits.",
  "journal.selective_breeding.seed_splicer_unlock": "The Seed Splicer is craftable starting from farming level {{level}}.\n\nTo get started, put five of a crop in each slot and click Splice. After a few hours the seeds will be ready to collect.",
  "journal.selective_breeding.mixing_heading": "Mixing Traits",
  "journal.selective_breeding.mixing": "When inputting two crops with traits, they will crossbreed and combine their traits into new seeds.\n\nEvery splice rolls its own result, so the same pair can give different seeds.\n\nWhen both crops share a trait at the same tier, there is a small chance it grows stronger.",
  "journal.selective_breeding.quality_hint": "[bounce][bold]Hint:[/bold][/bounce] The higher quality the crop, the more likely its traits are inherited!",
  "journal.selective_breeding.diluting_heading": "Diluting Traits",
  "journal.selective_breeding.diluting": "Got a trait you don't want? Splice the crop with a [link=baseline][underline]baseline[/underline][/link] crop of the same type.\n\nThis dilutes it, causing the removal of one of its traits or turning the seeds back to normal.\n\n[bounce][bold]Hint:[/bold][/bounce] The quality of both crops matters for preserving traits!",
  "journal.combination_traits.title": "Combination Traits",
  "journal.combination_traits.intro": "Some [link=trait][underline]traits[/underline][/link] can be mixed into a unique trait, called a [link=combination_traits][underline]combination trait[/underline][/link].\n\nWhen two crossbred crops each carry part of a required trait combination, there's a chance they combine into a single trait.\n\n[bounce][bold]Hint:[/bold][/bounce] Each half must come from a different parent. A crop that has both parts won't fuse on its own.",
  "journal.combination_traits.details": "A combination trait replaces the two traits that compose it. This can be helpful to bypass the three trait limit.\n\nA crop with a combination trait can still regain the traits it was made from. Their effects can stack with the combination's.\n\nSome combination traits can also turn a harmful trait into something useful!",
  "journal.traits.details_heading": "Details",
  "journal.traits.effects_heading": "Effects",
